1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,133
Curve Covenant helps a launch creator choose a bonding curve before deploying an xStock paired token.

2
00:00:06,083 --> 00:00:14,916
The product starts with a concrete decision: should a creator prioritize a smaller opening price jump, or a lower share of tokens going to early buyers?

3
00:00:14,916 --> 00:00:17,511
Those outcomes can conflict.

4
00:00:17,511 --> 00:00:23,464
Our initial customer hypothesis is launchpad teams and creators who need to review that choice.

5
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:32,987
Under an identical whale schedule, the long curve reduces the first price jump from three hundred eleven percent to two hundred thirty nine percent.

6
00:00:32,937 --> 00:00:38,390
But early buyers receive two point five three percentage points more of gross buy output.

7
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:41,592
The long curve also ends at a higher price.

8
00:00:41,592 --> 00:00:44,568
We show the cost alongside the benefit.

9
00:00:44,568 --> 00:00:49,723
This is a hypothetical result, not a promise of fairness or market performance.

10
00:00:50,881 --> 00:00:56,473
The product runs retail, whale, selling pressure, and graduation scenarios.

11
00:00:56,423 --> 00:01:02,269
Every transaction updates the next state, and sellers cannot sell tokens they do not hold.

12
00:01:02,269 --> 00:01:09,459
Builders inspect price paths, fees, costs, and reserves, then export the ledger or a visual report.

13
00:01:09,459 --> 00:01:15,602
The exact compared configuration can be passed to a wallet based launch and restored from a share link.

14
00:01:16,769 --> 00:01:21,409
Meteora DBC supplies the quote math and launch transactions.

15
00:01:21,359 --> 00:01:27,788
We independently checked the scenario state against fifty six executed swaps across eight local pools.

16
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:33,704
Prices, reserves, fees, balances, and transfers matched in integer units.

17
00:01:33,704 --> 00:01:40,597
The browser flow also created, bought, sold, refreshed balances, and graduated to DAMM version two.

18
00:01:40,597 --> 00:01:46,847
Public Phantom execution remains unverified; the stock balances in these tests are synthetic.

19
00:01:48,009 --> 00:01:55,161
The next distribution experiment is three to five observed trials with real launch creators or launchpad developers.

20
00:01:55,111 --> 00:01:59,349
We will measure whether a report changes their configuration decision.

21
00:01:59,349 --> 00:02:03,599
No adoption, revenue, or testimonials are claimed yet.

22
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:10,563
If teams need the comparison inside their own launchpad, an embeddable module is the next product hypothesis.

23
00:02:10,563 --> 00:02:15,218
Public wallet evidence and those user trials are the immediate priorities.
